'''''Cynanchica''''', commonly known as '''woodruff'',''''' is a [[genus]] of [[flowering plant]]s in the [[Family (taxonomy)|family]] [[Rubiaceae]]. It contains 73 species and has a wide distribution area from Europe, northern Africa, the Middle East and central Asia.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Cynanchica P.Caputo & Del Guacchio {{!}} Plants of the World Online {{!}} Kew Science |url=http://powo.science.kew.org/taxon/urn:lsid:ipni.org:names:77215273-1 |access-date=2024-08-01 |website=Plants of the World Online |language=en}}</ref> The genus was erected in 2020 to accommodate species split from the genus ''[[Asperula]]''.

